<speak>The layout is manageable when I have the full document open. The trouble comes when I move between the covering note and the attachments. I sometimes lose track of whether a paragraph is part of the formal document or simply an introductory explanation. Clear labels would help. I also prefer page references to instructions such as 'see below', because below means something different on a phone. I have made notes on a separate sheet rather than writing across the document. It keeps my questions separate from the wording I am reading.</speak>